    "content": "The current USS Kearsarge (LHD-3) is an active Wasp-class amphibious assault ship commissioned in 1993, designed to deploy Marines, helicopters, and landing craft. Known for humanitarian efforts, including Hurricane Katrina relief, she conducted F-35B operations in early 2026. As of Feb 2026, she is active in the Atlantic.Current Status and Known For (LHD-3):Mission: Known for amphibious assault, special operations, and humanitarian aid.Current Location: Recently active in the Atlantic Ocean conducting flight operations (as of Feb 2026).Key Capabilities: Carries MV-22 Ospreys, AH-64 Apache helicopters, and is capable of F-35B Lightning II landings.History Highlights: Rescued Capt. Scott O'Grady in 1995 and supported humanitarian efforts.Deployment History (LHD-3):1997: Evacuated non-combatants from Sierra Leone.2005: Provided disaster relief after Hurricane Katrina.Recent Years: Regular deployments to the Middle East and the Mediterranean.Other Ships Named Kearsarge:USS Kearsarge (1861): Famous Civil War sloop that sank the Confederate raider CSS Alabama in 1864.USS Kearsarge (BB-5): Battleship known for its unique \"double-stacked\" turrets, later a crane ship.USS Kearsarge (CV-33): Essex-class carrier that supported the Korean and Vietnam wars and served as a recovery ship for Mercury space missions.See the Wikipedia page and US Carriers.Net for more detailed history, or follow the official Instagram for recent updates.",
